    "http://ogp.me/ns#image": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "https://naccnaca-videos.s3.amazonaws.com/41937/rt_-_birch_bark_biting_yt_thumbnail_2__meta.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "Sisters Mairi and Claire Brascoupe from Kitigan Zibi shared their connection to the land from unceded Algonquin Territory. Mairi harvested birchbark, folding pieces before biting intricate patterns into them, and Claire sang while drumming. It was a shared experience that spoke directly to the history of those who lived and stewarded the land that Ottawa currently sits on.\n\nCredits \nArtist: Mairi Brascoupe \nSinger: Claire Brascoupe\n\n#ReconcileThis\n\nOver the last four years,..."
