        "@value": "John Storgårds became one of the world’s leading conductors almost by accident. He still travels everywhere with his violin. And his favourite composer is the one who trusts musicians enough not to tell them exactly what to do.\n\nLast fall, as John Storgårds returned to the National Arts Centre for his first concerts since being announced as Music Director Designate, journalist Paul Wells sat down with the Finnish maestro for a revealing conversation that went far beyond the..."
