        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "Moe Clark’s wîyâtikwêwin (Joy) moves between song and spoken word to trace joy, grief, and healing within Métis and 2Spirit communities. Through ceremony, language, and connection to land and ancestors, the piece honours Elders who hold teachings and make space for both pain and laughter. At the crossing of rivers where ancestral spaces awaken, communities gather to heal together and reclaim belonging.\n\nCredits\nby moe clark\nmusic by moe clark\nrecorded by moe clark..."
