        "@value": "Award-winning Cree writer, broadcaster, and poet Rosanna Deerchild has spent her life sharing Indigenous stories. As the daughter of a residential school survivor, she’s witnessed firsthand how trauma ripples through families—and how truth-telling can break those cycles. \n\nRosanna talks about her acclaimed play The Secret to Good Tea, how humour and storytelling help deal with pain and support healing, and why Indigenous voices are essential to Canada’s path toward..."
