    "http://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "A few things to know ...\n\n\n\tFrom tranquil visions of the Rhein River to dramatic shipwrecks along Canada’s Atlantic Coast, nature takes centre stage in all its beauty and power.\n\tCanadian maritime history comes alive in Kati Agócs’s Back to Elysium, which incorporates field recordings of Newfoundland fishing villages of the 1970s and ‘80s.\n\n\nAfter moving to Düsseldorf with his family in 1850, Robert Schumann’s long walks along the Rhine River provided a flood of inspiration for his Third Symphony, known as the “Rhenish.” A..."
      }
