    "http://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "We celebrate First Nations, Inuit, and Métis peoples, cultures, and perspectives in June and year-round.\n\nThis National Indigenous History Month, we spotlight Indigenous artists through a curated lineup of events, including performances, facilitator-led workshops, free powwow-themed programming, and the always lively Summer Indigenous Art Market.\n\nOn the Kipnes Lantern, naedè; migrating, a 3D-animated short film by Dene artist Casey Koyczan, fuses sci-fi aesthetics with traditional storytelling to challenge what a future might look like.\n\nJoin us online and in person at your National..."
      }
