    "http://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "It’s a Good Life If You Don’t Weaken is a rock concert wrapped in a play and a play wrapped up in a rock concert. It is a celebration of home and a love story about chosen family across borders, brought to life with the music of The Tragically Hip.\n\nSet in 2002, Waleed — an exiled journalist from Iraq — arrives in Canada and unexpectedly falls for Kate, the owner of a local music store. Their connection is immediate and undeniable. But when circumstances change, they are..."
      }
