    "http://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "We lose one another, find one another again, argue with one another, oppose one another, search for one another, neglect one another, and put up with one another. Often with great humility and vulnerability, we dare to believe in order to move forward. Our lives are filled with, sustained by, and woven around relationships, from friendships and family ties to romantic relationships. We have difficulty living without one another. Are our societies not founded on the notion (if not the imperative)..."
