      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "Sublimating hatred: that’s the shared ambition of singer-songwriter Safia Nolin and director Philippe Cyr. Together, they have compiled the thousands of genuine insults hurled at the singer and used them as raw material for an extraordinary musical work. What is the meaning of freedom of expression when it turns into violence?\n\nNolin courageously places herself at the centre of the show, in front of a large chorus that unleashes its venom on her. In a powerful celebration of..."
      }
