    "http://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "Both here and in the Colombian Amazon, the turtle is a central figure to many Indigenous cosmologies. Here the earth was created on a turtle’s back; there the turtle is the mother of all waters. The turtle is connected to the lunar cycle and the feminine side of life, in the water but also in the earth and the stars.\n\nNigamon and Tunai are the Anishinaabemowin and Inga words for “song.” Nigamon/Tunai is a poetic manifesto by Émilie Monnet and Waira Nina, inspired by the..."
      }
    ],
