    "http://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "Inspired by pagan processions, eleven performers tirelessly chant in a choir on stage, voicing a persistent prayer. At first plain and innocuous, the scene gradually becomes more complex, producing a near-psychedelic, hallucinogenic effect.\n\nWith ODE, Catherine Gaudet transports us to a surreal, exalted world, full of an extreme desire for harmony, coupled with palpable ambiguity. This forthcoming work from the innovative choreographer defies categorization with its compelling singularity,..."
      }
    ],
