    "http://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "Through history, personal stories and laughter, Mani Soleymanlou recreates for Canada’s Francophonie this plural and shifting discourse on language, migration and identity. A solo, a duet and then a chorus of 40 voices from the four corners of Canada, UN. DEUX. TROIS. delivers a polyphony of urgent humanity.\n\nTrois is a show that questions our roots and aspirations, what unites us and what and divides us, through the Russian nesting dolls of identity that..."
      }
