        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "Theatre Replacement has kept a small studio space in Vancouver’s Russian Hall since 2011. Some years ago, in a neighbouring closet, the company came across close to 20 hours of 16mm films sent from the USSR between the 1950s and 1980s. These slowly decomposing artifacts, many of them fragments, cover everything from heavy industry to demonstrations of folk dances. Drawing on this discovery as both a conceptual and aesthetic spark, Do you mind if I sit..."
