      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "Prototype is an international physical theatre production blending puppetry and cinematic storytelling to explore the enigma that is Jerzy Kosinski, the controversial Polish-American author of The Painted Bird and Being There. An exploration of ‘creative survival’ and an artist who was born out of trauma, the production repurposes events from Kosinski’s life and work and explores his lifelong re-imagining of reality - a survival response to the terrors he faced during..."
