        "@value": "The Music Circle: Fostering Musical Engagement for the Special Needs Community"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#image": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "https://cdn.nac-cna.ca/img/musiccircle/meta/musiccircle_meta_en.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "Some people might feel uncomfortable in settings with bright lights, crowds, or sudden loud noises. This can include people who are neurodivergent and/or have a disability. This can make it hard for them to enjoy music or events, especially concerts.\n\nThe Music Circle Program started in 2012. It was developed by the National Arts Centre team in collaboration with experts from Lotus Music, as well as occupational therapists and behavioural therapists.\n\nWe have developed a free guidebook and videos that can help everyone enjoy music. The information shows how we can create musical experiences that are enjoyable for people of all abilities, along with their families and caregivers. These resources will help you design an adaptive program that allows participants to learn about music in different ways and feel comfortable in the learning environment, regardless of their sensory needs. "
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns/fb#admins": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "728780803"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/en/musiccircle"
      }
    ]
  },
