  {
    "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/en/video/series/reconcilethis-fire-keepers",
    "http://ogp.me/ns/fb#app_id": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "123254964370141"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#type": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "article"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#url": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "https://nac-cna.ca/en/video/series/reconcilethis-fire-keepers"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#title": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "#ReconcileThis: Fire Keepers | Video series"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#image": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "https://naccnaca-series.s3.amazonaws.com/41934/reconcilethis-meta__meta.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "For the fourth year of #ReconcileThis, produced and curated by RJ Mitchell, Indigenous performance artists partnered with artisans to share stories representing the diverse cultures of Turtle Island, with artists from the West Coast, the Maritimes, the North, and the Ottawa Valley. Dancers, singers, and drummers worked alongside beaders, carvers, and weavers to create and share.\n\nTogether, these artists—the Fire Keepers—crafted work that spoke across mediums. Each material artist created a piece that told a story, then a performer brought it to life, giving voice to the work through performance.\n\n#ReconcileThis \n\nOver the last four years, #ReconcileThis has invited Indigenous artists to share their voices and perspectives through digital storytelling. Led by NAC Indigenous Theatre, the project is a space where reconciliation is carried through art, where communities are uplifted, and where Indigenous stories live online. \n\nYear 1: Fire Starters\n\nIn our first year, Fire Starters Sarain Fox, DJ Kookum, Isaac Murdoch, Sarah Podemski, Tamara Podemski, and Zoey Roy shared their inspiring messages on reconciliation. \n\nYear 2: Fire Carriers\n\nFor the second year of #ReconcileThis, established Indigenous artists – Fire Carriers – and young artists came together to share powerful stories from across Turtle Island.\n\nYear 3: Fire Tenders\n\nIn the third year of #ReconcileThis, artists from across disciplines and generations came together to reflect on reconciliation through the theme of Joy and Mischief. "
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns/fb#admins": [
