      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#title": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "#ReconcileThis: Fire Tenders | Video series"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#image": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "https://naccnaca-series.s3.amazonaws.com/39905/reconcilethis-meta__meta.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "In the third year of #ReconcileThis, led by Philip Geller, artists from across disciplines and generations came together to reflect on reconciliation through the theme of Joy and Mischief. Its spark came from recorded conversations of cross-generational visits with the Fire Tenders. Those encounters inspired a series of video shorts.\n\nIn its final expression, the Fire Tenders are creating dance, theatre, film, music, spoken word, and more, weaving generations together through visits filled with joy and mischief.\n \n\n#ReconcileThis: Fire Starters\n\nIn our first year, Fire Starters Sarain Fox, DJ Kookum, Isaac Murdoch, Sarah Podemski, Tamara Podemski, and Zoey Roy shared their inspiring messages on reconciliation. \n\n#ReconcileThis: Fire Carriers\n\nFor the second year of #ReconcileThis, established Indigenous artists – Fire Carriers – and young artists came together to share powerful stories from across Turtle Island."
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns/fb#admins": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "728780803"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/en/video/series/reconcilethis-fire-tenders"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/en/video/series/naco-mentorship-talks-masterclasses",
    "http://ogp.me/ns/fb#app_id": [
