    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Hailing from British Columbia, Raven Grenier, Bill Barnes, and Adanchilla Pauls Lepine created beautiful pieces shown in the performance Wolverine. Adanchilla beaded a formline heart as the centerpiece for the performance while Bill and Raven worked decorative chains into the outfits and hairstyling of the performers. Wolverine was performed by Raven and Aysha Alfred, telling the story of the Wolverine, passed down for generations on the West Coast. Credits Director, Choreographer, Performer: Raven Grenier Performer: Aysha Alfred Music: Raven Grenier & plant daddy Bodychains, Jewelry: Raven Grenier & homohardware Beadwork, Formline Heart Design: Adanchilla Pauls Lepine Animation, Video Design: Andrew Moro Videographer, Technical Director: Andrew Grenier Hair Styling, Braidwork: Kenidy Crouter Costuming, Technician: Bill Barnes Dramaturgy: Margaret Grenier Partner, Venue: Ballet BC #ReconcileThis Over the last four years, #ReconcileThis has invited Indigenous artists to share their voices and perspectives through digital storytelling. Led by NAC Indigenous Theatre, the project is a space where reconciliation is carried through art, where communities are uplifted, and where Indigenous stories live online. For the fourth year of #ReconcileThis, produced and curated by RJ Mitchell, Indigenous performance artists partnered with artisans to share stories representing the diverse cultures of Turtle Island, with artists from the West Coast, the Maritimes, the North, and the Ottawa Valley. Dancers, singers, and drummers worked alongside beaders, carvers, and weavers to create and share."
      }
