    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "From the Mohawk community of Akwesasne, Carrie Hill and Feryn King combined their skills in basket weaving and hoop dancing to share their heritage, as well as their artistic journeys. Carrie wove black ash splints into a beautiful basket while Feryn used her hoops and movements inspired by weaving techniques to breathe life into it. Video credits Weaver: Carrie Hill Dancer: Feryn King Videographer: Brittany Bonaparte Music “Imiq” Performed by Tanya Tagaq Written by Tanya Tagaq, Jean Martin, Celina Kalluk, Patrick O’Reilly Published by Songs of Six Shooter B (SOCAN), Jean Martin, Celina Kalluk, Patrick O’Reilly Courtesy of Six Shooter Records, © 2026 #ReconcileThis Over the last four years, #ReconcileThis has invited Indigenous artists to share their voices and perspectives through digital storytelling. Led by NAC Indigenous Theatre, the project is a space where reconciliation is carried through art, where communities are uplifted, and where Indigenous stories live online. For the fourth year of #ReconcileThis, produced and curated by RJ Mitchell, Indigenous performance artists partnered with artisans to share stories representing the diverse cultures of Turtle Island, with artists from the West Coast, the Maritimes, the North, and the Ottawa Valley. Dancers, singers, and drummers worked alongside beaders, carvers, and weavers to create and share."
      }
    ]
