    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Jaime Morse is a Métis artist who resides in Ottawa, along with her son, Jacob McKenzie, as they bring Métis art online. Jaime designs moccasin vamps that incorporate her family’s connection to the land, to be decorated using fish scales. Jacob demonstrates the Métis-style jigging that is widely renowned throughout Turtle Island. Credits Artist: Jaime Morse Dancer: Jacob McKenzie #ReconcileThis Over the last four years, #ReconcileThis has invited Indigenous artists to share their voices and perspectives through digital storytelling. Led by NAC Indigenous Theatre, the project is a space where reconciliation is carried through art, where communities are uplifted, and where Indigenous stories live online. For the fourth year of #ReconcileThis, produced and curated by RJ Mitchell, Indigenous performance artists partnered with artisans to share stories representing the diverse cultures of Turtle Island, with artists from the West Coast, the Maritimes, the North, and the Ottawa Valley. Dancers, singers, and drummers worked alongside beaders, carvers, and weavers to create and share."
