  {
    "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/genid/5073442994f030f5",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/VideoObject"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/thumbnailUrl": [
      {
        "@id": "https://naccnaca-videos.s3.amazonaws.com/41911/creation-fund---mahabharata---lpl-2__large.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/uploadDate": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2026-08-04T13:48:00-04:00"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/en/video/national-creation-fund-supporting-artistic-risk-taking"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Supporting artistic risk-taking "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "&ldquo;Having someone believe in your project before it is what it is, means&nbsp;everything as an artist and it has changed my life.&nbsp;The National Creation Fund goes to the roots of the ecosystem, who are often the people who are taking the biggest risks.&rdquo; &ndash; Miriam&#8239;Fernandes, co-creator of&nbsp;Mahabharata&nbsp; In this interview, Miriam&#8239;Fernandes talks about&nbsp;Why Not Theatre&rsquo;s stage adaptation of&nbsp;Mahabharata,&nbsp;a 4000-year-old Sanskrit epic that is foundational to South Asian culture. This uniquely ambitious, large-scale production&nbsp;received&nbsp;investment&nbsp;from the National Creation Fund from the&nbsp;outset and&nbsp;has since toured to prestigious stages around the world.&nbsp;The co-creator, Miriam Fernandes emphasizes that the Fund&rsquo;s&nbsp;support was crucial in&nbsp;allowing&nbsp;the&nbsp;creative team&nbsp;to take risks that would otherwise have been impossible.&nbsp; Mahabharata&nbsp;is&nbsp;one of&nbsp;nearly 120&#8239;works&nbsp;supported by the Fund. It was presented&nbsp;at&nbsp;the NAC as part of English Theatre&rsquo;s 2024&ndash;2025&#8239;season.&nbsp; The Fund empowers Canadian artists to embrace creative risks, explore new forms and make their most ambitious dreams a reality, resulting in innovative performances that are enjoyed by audiences across Canada and abroad. The National Creation Fund is powered by philanthropy. Thank you to our donors for making it possible. Learn more: National Creation Fund"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/genid/8c027729a31df2ad",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/VideoObject"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/thumbnailUrl": [
      {
        "@id": "https://naccnaca-videos.s3.amazonaws.com/41864/creation-fund---murmuration---lpl_no-logo__large.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/uploadDate": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2026-07-17T10:09:00-04:00"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/en/video/national-creation-fund-supporting-the-future-of-an-art-form"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Supporting the future of an art form"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "&ldquo;Thanks to the support of the National Creation Fund, we were able to grow and take a step towards large scale choreography, which otherwise would never have been possible.&rdquo; &ndash; Alexandre Hamel, Skating Artist, Choreographer, Founder and Artistic Director In this interview,&nbsp; Alexandre Hamel discusses Le Patin Libre&rsquo;s Murmuration, a piece whose choreography is inspired by the flight of birds. He also talks about his ambition to develop a new art form and pass it on to the next generation of skaters. He highlights the support of the National Arts Centre&rsquo;s National Creation Fund, which provided his company with the resources and time needed to bring this ambitious production to life.&nbsp; Murmuration is one of nearly 120 works supported by the Fund, and it was presented at the NAC as part of NAC Dance&rsquo;s 2024&ndash;2025 season. &nbsp; The Fund empowers Canadian artists to embrace creative risks, explore new forms and make their most ambitious dreams a reality, resulting in innovative performances that are enjoyed by audiences across Canada and abroad. &nbsp; The National Creation Fund is powered by philanthropy. Thank you to our donors for making it possible. Learn more: National Creation Fund"
      }
    ]
  },
