    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "A creative tour in the heart of the Far North"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "In the winter of 2026, musician Zac Hackett and Inuit throat singer Olivia Chislett travelled to the Northwest Territories and Yukon as part of the Northern Youth Creative Tour. Over a two-week period, the two teaching artists, in collaboration with Arts Alive, offered workshops, performances, and creative activities focused on music and cultural exchange to young people in Yellowknife, Whitehorse, and Dawson City. Through musical improvisation, songwriting, and throat singing, youth participants were able to explore their creativity, expand their artistic knowledge, and build connections within their communities, all in a safe environment. In this interview, Zac and Olivia work with young people at the Home Base Youth Centre in Yellowknife and talk about this free program, which Arts Alive has supported for several years."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
