    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "In Honour of Her, A Loveletter to Aki"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Emily Marie Seguin&rsquo;s live audio recordings taken from throughout the Ottawa downtown core create a dense composition, accompanied by memories from Jennifer Ferrante that recount a Mother and Daughter&rsquo;s relationship to the territory and calls to the importance of the wellness of Aki. Location: The Gather-Ring, Portage Bridge, Ottawa, Ontario Credits Emily Marie Seguin Interpreted from a Memory from Jennifer Ferrante&nbsp; Dawn Seguin, Live Audio Capture Brit Johnston, Artist Liaison Howard Adler, Videographer&nbsp; Jaime Morse, Consulting (Ottawa) Heather Cant, Consulting (Indigenous Cities) &nbsp; Indigenous Cities: The stories here. Experience stories from the cities you thought you knew &ndash; Montreal, Vancouver, Saskatoon, and Ottawa. Indigenous Cities presents memories from Indigenous community members based in cities across Canada; memories that have been interpreted by Indigenous artists to create a unique audio storytelling experience.&nbsp; Learn more:&nbsp;Indigenous Cities Ottawa&nbsp;"
      }
    ]
  },
