        "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/en/video/indigenous-cities-vancouver-i-am-here-grandmother-olivia-c-davies"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "I Am Here Grandmother"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "In I Am Here Grandmother, Rosemary Georgeson tells the story of how childhood memories and the Firehall Arts Centre led her to reclaiming four generations of her family, all propelled by the love for her great grandmother. Location: Firehall Arts Centre / Old No. 1 Firehall, 280 E. Cordova Street, Vancouver, B.C. Credits Interpreted from a Memory from Rosemary Georgeson&nbsp; Additional words: Olivia C. Davies&nbsp; Music: &ldquo;Alpha&rdquo; and &ldquo;Rematriate&rdquo; by Michael Red, remixed by Olivia C. Davies&nbsp; SAVAGE SOCIETY&nbsp; (Vancouver) Darylina Powderface, community engagement coordinator&nbsp; Cameron Peal, production coordination&nbsp; Sherri Sadler, marketing &amp; communications&nbsp; Chelsea Carlson, production management&nbsp; Safoura Rigi-Ladiz, copywriting and videography Heather Cant, consulting (Indigenous Cities)&nbsp; &nbsp; Indigenous Cities: The stories here. Experience stories from the cities you thought you knew &ndash; Montreal, Vancouver, Saskatoon, and Ottawa. Indigenous Cities presents memories from Indigenous community members based in cities across Canada; memories that have been interpreted by Indigenous artists to create a unique audio storytelling experience.&nbsp; Learn more:&nbsp;Indigenous Cities Vancouver&nbsp;"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/genid/853ada3ea5f5b816",
