    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "#ReconcileThis: Frog Hunt"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Natalie Sappier&rsquo;s Frog Hunt follows Jaxon and Justin as they wait for nighttime and prepare for their adventure. Wearing glow sticks that create silhouettes in the dark, they play and search together, capturing the imagination and freedom of childhood. Credits Film by Samaqani Cocahaq and Carr Sappier-Paul Actors: Justin and Jaxon Finnemore Music by M3D14: Static Mind and Flourishing Love Filmed in Neqotkuk (Tobique First Nation), NB &nbsp; #ReconcileThis Since 2021, #ReconcileThis has invited Indigenous artists to share their voices and perspectives through digital storytelling. Led by NAC Indigenous Theatre in collaboration with Meta, the project is a space where reconciliation is carried through art, where communities are uplifted, and where Indigenous stories live online. Now, in its third year, #ReconcileThis turns to the theme of joy and mischief. Led by Red River Michif and Jewish theatre artist Philip Geller, this season shares the laughter, teasing, and playful resilience that connect communities across generations."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/genid/2bbabeb6cefe70fd",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/VideoObject"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/thumbnailUrl": [
      {
        "@id": "https://naccnaca-videos.s3.amazonaws.com/40251/reconcile-this-questions__large.jpg"
