        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2025-12-19T14:07:00-05:00"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/en/video/reconcilethis-questions-grass-way-forward"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "#ReconcileThis: Questions, Grass, and the Way Forward"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Baby Trickster presents a multimedia performance piece that traces journeys through friendship, identity, and colonial violence. Through spoken word and fragmented dialogue, the collective addresses the sacred meaning of braids in Indigenous culture and poses questions about resilience and the future. Credits Created and performed by Sage Boulanger McLeod Mary Catagas Keely McPeek&nbsp; Mady Richard Kathleen Starr Tyler Shingoose Directed by:&nbsp;Philip Geller Music&nbsp; Resolved by Greyson Roy Gritt and Bryden Gwiss Kiwenzie&nbsp; Memories of Summer by Justin Delorme&nbsp; Slowdance by Evan Micheal Pang and Tasheena Lynn Sarazin &nbsp; #ReconcileThis Since 2021, #ReconcileThis has invited Indigenous artists to share their voices and perspectives through digital storytelling. Led by NAC Indigenous Theatre in collaboration with Meta, the project is a space where reconciliation is carried through art, where communities are uplifted, and where Indigenous stories live online. Now, in its third year, #ReconcileThis turns to the theme of joy and mischief. Led by Red River Michif and Jewish theatre artist Philip Geller, this season shares the laughter, teasing, and playful resilience that connect communities across generations."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/genid/240fa1daba0d53b3",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/VideoObject"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/thumbnailUrl": [
      {
        "@id": "https://naccnaca-videos.s3.amazonaws.com/40250/reconcile-this-jaeli__large.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/uploadDate": [
