        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2025-12-19T14:07:00-05:00"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/en/video/reconcilethis-jaeli-bruno"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "#ReconcileThis: Cosmic Birth"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Jaeli Bruno shares a spoken word poem about a spirit&rsquo;s journey from the cosmos into earthly life. Through imagery of northern lights, ancestral beings, and the Seventh Fire, she reflects on themes of birth, memory, and the guidance that accompanies us into this world. Created and performed by Jaeli Bruno &nbsp; #ReconcileThis Since 2021, #ReconcileThis has invited Indigenous artists to share their voices and perspectives through digital storytelling. Led by NAC Indigenous Theatre in collaboration with Meta, the project is a space where reconciliation is carried through art, where communities are uplifted, and where Indigenous stories live online. Now, in its third year, #ReconcileThis turns to the theme of joy and mischief. Led by Red River Michif and Jewish theatre artist Philip Geller, this season shares the laughter, teasing, and playful resilience that connect communities across generations."
      }
    ]
