        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "#ReconcileThis: Family of Tricksters"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Issa Kixen and family share stories of trickster moments, from Ron&rsquo;s winter night adventure to Alfie&rsquo;s chaotic Christmas party, and other memories from Fort Frances and Couchiching First Nation, where summer days at the Point and Canada Day feasts shaped a connection to land, family, and storytelling. Credits Narrators: Issa Kixen and Isaac Leforte First story: Ron Kixen Second story: Alfie Kixen Third story: Gail Roach-Leforte #ReconcileThis Since 2021, #ReconcileThis has invited Indigenous artists to share their voices and perspectives through digital storytelling. Led by NAC Indigenous Theatre in collaboration with Meta, the project is a space where reconciliation is carried through art, where communities are uplifted, and where Indigenous stories live online. Now, in its third year, #ReconcileThis turns to the theme of joy and mischief. Led by Red River Michif and Jewish theatre artist Philip Geller, this season shares the laughter, teasing, and playful resilience that connect communities across generations."
      }
