    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Mariel Belanger&rsquo;s The Reeds Remember reflects on connection to land and the work of creating home and belonging across generations. Through the patient act of gathering what the earth offers, spaces are made and held for those who come after, tending to what endures. Credits A film by Mariel Belanger Performance co-created with Kalli Van Stone English poem by Mariel Belanger Cattail and sand plant drawings and N&#39;sylxcen song by Kalli Van Stone Music generated by AI Studio s&iacute;spik&nbsp; &nbsp; #ReconcileThis Since 2021, #ReconcileThis has invited Indigenous artists to share their voices and perspectives through digital storytelling. Led by NAC Indigenous Theatre in collaboration with Meta, the project is a space where reconciliation is carried through art, where communities are uplifted, and where Indigenous stories live online. Now, in its third year, #ReconcileThis turns to the theme of joy and mischief. Led by Red River Michif and Jewish theatre artist Philip Geller, this season shares the laughter, teasing, and playful resilience that connect communities across generations."
      }
