    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Christine Genier&rsquo;s poem What We Learn from the Road traces memories of highway drives with family through the changing seasons of the North. Genier reflects on conversations with her grandmother about D&auml;n k&rsquo;e (the ways of the people), the persistence of language, and the teachings that sustain Indigenous communities across generations. Created and performed by Christine Genier &nbsp; #ReconcileThis Since 2021, #ReconcileThis has invited Indigenous artists to share their voices and perspectives through digital storytelling. Led by NAC Indigenous Theatre in collaboration with Meta, the project is a space where reconciliation is carried through art, where communities are uplifted, and where Indigenous stories live online. Now, in its third year, #ReconcileThis turns to the theme of joy and mischief. Led by Red River Michif and Jewish theatre artist Philip Geller, this season shares the laughter, teasing, and playful resilience that connect communities across generations."
      }
    ]
