    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "#ReconcileThis: You Can’t Have One Without The Other"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "&acirc;pihtawikosis&acirc;niskw&ecirc;w (M&eacute;tis/mixed-settler) multidisciplinary artist and 2Spirit singing thunderbird Moe Clark gathered in a tipi on the 2Spirit Sundance grounds at Medicine Wolf Healing Place (Long Plains First Nation) with respected 2Spirit Elders Barbara Bruce and Charlotte Nolin. Together they visited about 2Spirit joy and resilience through community and kinship. From that spark, nehiyaw artist and filmmaker Tyson Houseman created a video reminding us of the enduring strength of 2Spirit communities and their essential place in a healthy society. &nbsp; #ReconcileThis Since 2021, #ReconcileThis has invited Indigenous artists to share their voices and perspectives through digital storytelling. Led by NAC Indigenous Theatre in collaboration with Meta, the project is a space where reconciliation is carried through art, where communities are uplifted, and where Indigenous stories live online. Now, in its third year, #ReconcileThis turns to the theme of joy and mischief. Led by Red River Michif and Jewish theatre artist Philip Geller, this season shares the laughter, teasing, and playful resilience that connect communities across generations."
      }
    ]
