    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Syilx interdisciplinary performance artist Mariel Belanger travelled with her cousin, Kalli Van Stone, through Otter Lake, British Columbia, near Okanagan Indian Band Reserve #2, reflecting on the power of our relationship to the land. From that spark, Claire Brascoup&eacute; created a video that highlights the countless teachings the land offers when we pause and listen, and our responsibility to share those teachings across generations. &nbsp; #ReconcileThis Since 2021, #ReconcileThis has invited Indigenous artists to share their voices and perspectives through digital storytelling. Led by NAC Indigenous Theatre in collaboration with Meta, the project is a space where reconciliation is carried through art, where communities are uplifted, and where Indigenous stories live online. Now, in its third year, #ReconcileThis turns to the theme of joy and mischief. Led by Red River Michif and Jewish theatre artist Philip Geller, this season shares the laughter, teasing, and playful resilience that connect communities across generations."
      }
