    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Jaeli Bruno shared a video chat with her sister filled with playful pranks, sibling teasing, and rare moments of honesty. Video maker Tyson Houseman transformed that conversation into a short film that carries the energy of sibling bonds and the resilience found in laughter. &nbsp; #ReconcileThis Since 2021, #ReconcileThis has invited Indigenous artists to share their voices and perspectives through digital storytelling. Led by NAC Indigenous Theatre in collaboration with Meta, the project is a space where reconciliation is carried through art, where communities are uplifted, and where Indigenous stories live online. Now, in its third year, #ReconcileThis turns to the theme of joy and mischief. Led by Red River Michif and Jewish theatre artist Philip Geller, this season shares the laughter, teasing, and playful resilience that connect communities across generations."
