        "@value": "#ReconcileThis: Young Explorers"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Wolastoqey multidisciplinary storyteller Samaqani Cocahq-Natalie Sappier of Neqotkuk First Nation, New Brunswick, spoke by phone with her sister, Carr Niponahtuwess Sappier-Paul, about the next generation and building joyful, abundant spaces for the future. From that spark, Mi&rsquo;kmaq animator and multidisciplinary artist Alan Syliboy created a video reminding us to think seven generations ahead, knowing everything we do today affects those who follow. #ReconcileThis Since 2021, #ReconcileThis has invited Indigenous artists to share their voices and perspectives through digital storytelling. Led by NAC Indigenous Theatre in collaboration with Meta, the project is a space where reconciliation is carried through art, where communities are uplifted, and where Indigenous stories live online. Now, in its third year, #ReconcileThis turns to the theme of joy and mischief. Led by Red River Michif and Jewish theatre artist Philip Geller, this season shares the laughter, teasing, and playful resilience that connect communities across generations."
