        "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/en/video/creation-fund-100th-investment"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The National Creation Fund's 100th investment"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The NAC&rsquo;s National Creation Fund, a catalyst for the creation of major works in Canada, has just celebrated the milestone of its 100th investment in a Canadian production, with its support of Empire of Wild, by the Canadian Opera Company and co-produced by the National Arts Centre Orchestra and Indigenous Theatre. These 100 productions represent the thousands of companies, artists, and communities across this country who continue to create despite innumerable challenges. Who understand that creation is a force of joy and resistance. Whose dedication to offering their wildest dreams to our communities is breathtaking. The National Creation Fund is our gift to these artists, and the audiences who cherish them.&nbsp; For the occasion, we have given the floor to artists who have received the support from the National Creation Fund.&nbsp; Video: Samuel Vincent Coombes Illustrations: Mairi &amp; Simon Brascoup&eacute;"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/genid/4bc9beec8b0507ba",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/VideoObject"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/thumbnailUrl": [
      {
        "@id": "https://naccnaca-videos.s3.amazonaws.com/39626/interlude_2__large.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/uploadDate": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2025-08-25T09:29:00-04:00"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/en/video/interlude"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Interlude by Virginie Brunelle"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Interlude is a creation in situ that unfolds in a series of eight fragments, each reflecting a unique facet of the complexity and magic of human relationships. Through these fragments, the choreography explores the multiple angles of love, that irresistible call to live and weave deep bonds with each other. Incommunicability, one of our society&rsquo;s contemporary ills, inhabits the protagonists&rsquo; bodies, revealing awkwardness and relational fears that camouflage their desire for sincere connection. Always anchored in a vital momentum, in&nbsp;Interlude love continues to serve as Virginie&rsquo;s creative beacon, illuminating her artistic universe with raw, emotional sincerity. This performance of Interlude took place in the Peter A. Herrndorf Place at the National Arts Centre on February 26, 2025. Interlude is an NAC Dance commission. Choreographer: Virginie Brunelle Dancers: Caroline Namts and Danny De Matos Music: Pietro Antonio Locatelli, Concerti Grossi, Op. 1, Nos 1-6"
      }
    ]
  },
