  {
    "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/genid/d40c3a5b4f99129c",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/VideoObject"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/thumbnailUrl": [
      {
        "@id": "https://naccnaca-videos.s3.amazonaws.com/39553/1_elgin_charcuterie_tutorial_copy_06.00_11_08_07.still006__large.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/uploadDate": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2025-07-31T14:19:00-04:00"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/en/video/charcuterie-cocktails-thatll-steal-the-show-an-nac-chef-series-recipe"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Charcuterie and cocktails that’ll steal the show"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "We&rsquo;re showcasing the creation of a stunning charcuterie board &mdash; perfect for entertaining, impressing guests, or just treating yourself to something beautiful and delicious. Pair it with an easy sip &mdash; try our signature 1 Elgin Tonic or the vibrant Violet Vibe cocktail! Cocktails 1Elgin tonic - 0.5 oz lemon juice - 0.5 oz rosemary syrup - Fill &frac34; of the cup with tonic water - Top with 1.5 oz Empress Gin Violet Vibe - 1 oz Vodka - 0.5 oz Cherry Whiskey - 0.5 oz blue Curacao - 0.5 oz simple syrup - 0.5 oz lemon juice Simple syrup 1 part sugar one part water (for more liquid syrup) 2 part sugar one part water (a bit more consistency) :: Charcuterie Board for 6 People :: Planning the layout Choose a large platter or board: (wooden, marble, slate, or a combination). Arrange items in sections: cheeses, meats, fruits, nuts, crackers, spreads. Create visual interest: use height (small bowls, stacked items) and varied shapes/colours. Selection of cheeses (3-4 varieties) Soft cheeses: Brie, Camembert, or Goat cheese. Hard cheeses: Aged Cheddar, Manchego, Gruy&egrave;re. Blue cheese: Gorgonzola or Roquefort (optional). &bull; Pre-slice or leave some whole for presentation. &bull; Offer a variety of textures and flavors. &nbsp; Selection of meats (3-4 varieties) Cured meats:&nbsp;Salami (spicy or mild),&nbsp;Prosciutto, Chorizo, Soppressata &bull; Roll or fold slices for a neat look. &bull; Place meats in clusters or overlapping stacks. &nbsp; Fresh and dried fruits Fresh fruits: Grapes, figs, apple or pear slices, berries. Dried fruits: Apricots, cranberries, dates. &bull; Use seasonal fruits. &bull; Wash and dry thoroughly. Nuts and spreads Nuts: Almonds, walnuts, pistachios. Spreads: Honey, fig jam, almond butter, mustard. &bull; Place spreads in small bowls. &bull; Include a honey dipper or small knives. Crackers and breads Crackers: Assorted (plain, seeded, multigrain). Breads: Baguette slices, breadsticks. &bull; Arrange around the board edges. &bull; Pre-slice for easy serving. Garnishes and extras Olives: Green, Kalamata, stuffed. Pickles: Cornichons, pickled onions. Fresh herbs: Rosemary, thyme for visual appeal. Cheese knives &amp; small spoons for serving. Additional tips &bull; Balance flavours: salty, sweet, savory, tangy. &bull; Vary textures: creamy, crunchy, chewy. &bull; Colourful presentation: contrasting colours make it appealing. Quantity estimate: Cheeses: 4-6 oz per person (~24 oz total). Meats: 2-3 oz per person (~12 oz total). Fruits/nuts: enough to complement (about 1-2 cups each). Crackers/breads: enough for 6 people (~15-20 pieces). Final touches &bull; Add small labels for cheeses and meats if desired. &bull; Keep the board accessible and inviting. &bull; Serve at room temperature for optimal flavor. The NAC&#39;s mandate has always been to nurture and support performing artists from across Canada. Our 1 Elgin Resident Chef program creates a \"stage\" for Canada&#39;s most promising culinary artists to share their knowledge and innovation, as well as regional and cultural foods that they love.&nbsp;"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/genid/a74e73d9feed7313",
