        "@value": "2025-06-26T15:24:00-04:00"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/en/video/the-sweet-side-of-parsnip"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The sweet side of parsnip: An NAC Chef series recipe"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Originally from Vancouver, BC, Celeste Mah was recognized as Canada&rsquo;s Best Pastry Chef in 2019. Her innovative approach to flavour pairings and texture has led her to create desserts from the unexpected. Chef Celeste Mah was the Resident Chef from March through May 2025 along with her husband and business partner Chef Ross Larkin. Together they own Portage restaurant in historic downtown St John&rsquo;s, Newfoundland.&nbsp; The NAC&#39;s mandate has always been to nurture and support performing artists from across Canada. Our 1 Elgin Resident Chef program creates a &ldquo;stage&rdquo; for Canada&#39;s most promising culinary artists to share their knowledge and innovation, as well as regional and cultural foods that they love.&nbsp;"
      }
    ]
  },
