    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/en/video/nac-chef-series-simple-jerk-spice-with-salmon"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Simple Jerk Spice with Salmon: An NAC Chef Series Recipe"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Chef Kenton Leier cooks an inspired Caribbean dish with resident chef Resa Solomon-St. Lewis. Chef Resa also explains how to make a great jerk sauce that they used to accompany the salmon they made in this video. Chef Resa Solomon-St. Lewis was the Resident Chef from January to March 2025.&nbsp; 1 Elgin Jerk Sauce The spicy, smoky aromatic flavours of this sauce make it a great choice for chicken, pork, or fish. Ingredients (yield 500 ml) 1 small white onion, minced 1 Tbsp&nbsp;sea salt &frac12; bunch fresh thyme, chopped&nbsp; 6 cloves fresh garlic, finely chopped&nbsp; 1 Tbsp ginger, finely grated&nbsp; 1 tsp cinnamon powder&nbsp; 2 tsp All spice, ground 1 tsp pepper, ground&nbsp; &frac12; tsp nutmeg, ground&nbsp; 2 Tbsp&nbsp;brown sugar 2 Tbsp honey&nbsp; 2 Tbsp soy sauce&nbsp; 1-2 Scotch Bonnet peppers (depending on heat preference), seeds removed and finely chopped&nbsp; &frac14; cup vegetable oil &frac14; cup lime juice Preparation: Combine all the above ingredients together and store in an airtight container at room temperature. Resident Chef Program The NAC&rsquo;s mandate has always been to nurture and support a diverse assemblage of performing artists from across Canada. We&rsquo;re proud to present the Resident Chef program, with the intention of creating a stage for Canada&rsquo;s most promising culinary artists.&nbsp;"
      }
    ]
  },
