      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/en/video/vancouver-reconcilethis-2024"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "#ReconcileThis Vancouver"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "In Vancouver, Kelsey Wavey led a project centered around their journey of reclaiming and sharing their gift of song. Give It Up / Give It Back&nbsp;reflects on Wavey&rsquo;s early experiences with the residential school apology and their first protest at age 15. The video combines personal reflection with a powerful song about land, renewal, and the role of art in decolonization and cultural reclamation."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/genid/10337ac83b7ef8a7",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/VideoObject"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/thumbnailUrl": [
      {
        "@id": "https://naccnaca-videos.s3.amazonaws.com/37762/rt-timmins_still__large.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/uploadDate": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2024-12-12T16:27:00-05:00"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/en/video/timmins-reconcilethis-2024"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "#ReconcileThis Timmins"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "In Timmins, Mike Metawabin collaborated with Simon Amb&uuml;hl and Dr. Manuel Menrath to create a powerful audiovisual experience. His poem, &ldquo;Hounds of St. Anne&rsquo;s,&rdquo; was paired with music to reflect on the deep impact of residential schools. The project evolved into Songs of the Land,&nbsp;a transatlantic collaboration blending poetry, music, and visual storytelling to address cultural trauma and healing."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/genid/6a53b69fb5a4b8dc",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/VideoObject"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/thumbnailUrl": [
      {
        "@id": "https://naccnaca-videos.s3.amazonaws.com/37761/rt-regina_composite-still__large.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/uploadDate": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2024-12-12T16:27:00-05:00"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/en/video/regina-reconcilethis-2024"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "#ReconcileThis Regina"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "In Regina, Skyler Anderson worked with Treaty 4 youth Jaycee Anderson and Kiana Toto to create compelling art that addresses the challenges of living in a colonial world. The youth reflected on the differences between the world of their ancestors and their own, using ceremony and cultural expression to make sense of their identity in today&rsquo;s society. Their work highlights the importance of culture, identity, and tradition in the modern world."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/genid/c3c82a04d13f07c2",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/VideoObject"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/thumbnailUrl": [
      {
        "@id": "https://naccnaca-videos.s3.amazonaws.com/37760/rt-edmonton_still__large.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/uploadDate": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2024-12-12T16:27:00-05:00"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/en/video/edmonton-reconcilethis-2024"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "#ReconcileThis Edmonton"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "In Edmonton, Barry Bilinski and Todd Houseman worked with youth from Treaty 6, Joshua Carter-Killback, Kingston Ward-Bouvier, and Eden Mayes, to create a video collage focused on the future of Indigenous nations. Guided by the wisdom of Elders, the youth shared their visions of a thriving cultural future. The resulting video is a powerful expression of hope, creativity, and a forward-looking vision, rooted in cultural teachings and traditions."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/genid/79cb5815fe30f5ab",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/VideoObject"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/thumbnailUrl": [
      {
        "@id": "https://naccnaca-videos.s3.amazonaws.com/37597/r-i_botis__large.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/uploadDate": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2024-10-22T11:52:00-04:00"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/en/video/interview-with-far-from-the-norms-botis-seva-entrevue-avec-botis-seva"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Interview with Far From The Norm's Botis Seva "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "In this interview, NAC Senior Strategist for Audience Engagement Rose-Ingrid Benjamin sat down with artistic director and choreographer Botis Seva about his story and journey to dance, how he overcame adversity, and his inspirations for his piece BLKDOG.&nbsp; Vital and gripping,&#8239;BLKDOG&nbsp;is Botis Seva&rsquo;s Olivier award-winning Hip Hop dance-theatre production was presented at the NAC on October 23 and 24, 2024."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/genid/5fddf46ae0262fd3",
