  {
    "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/genid/46bbc65259272719",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/VideoObject"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/thumbnailUrl": [
      {
        "@id": "https://naccnaca-videos.s3.amazonaws.com/37348/tamara-podemski-screenshot__large.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/uploadDate": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2024-09-26T08:54:00-04:00"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/en/video/tamara-podemski-reconcilethis"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Tamara Podemski: Artist, Storyteller, Fire starter"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "#ReconcileThis is a movement to activate and uplift Indigenous Voices by lighting a social media fire of conversations and celebrations of culture through digital stories, songs, dance.&nbsp; Tamara Podemski shares a song of healing and hope, envisioning a &ldquo;brand new day&rdquo; for her family and survivors of residential schools. &ldquo;I am the granddaughter of two residential school survivors &ndash; Tom Anaquod and Sophie McDonald. They met at LeBret Indian Residential School in the Qu&rsquo;Appelle Valley, Saskatchewan. I wrote a song in honour of them called &ldquo;Brand New Day,&rdquo; which I performed at the inaugural event of the Truth and Reconciliation Commission in Winnipeg back in 2010. Over a decade later, I&rsquo;m still singing the song and yet, these past couple years, it seems to resonate now more than ever. Sharing this song with my family and singing it with my son, in particular, inspired me to explore how lyrics &ndash; heard or sung through music &ndash; can allow people to access complex emotions and ideas and maybe even experience them in a more supported and compassionate way. How can we carry the painful truths of our stories, while also celebrating our own existences in spite of everything?&rdquo; #ReconcileThis @thetamarapodemski:&nbsp;Original #ReconcileThis post on Instagram"
      }
    ]
  },
